    "body": "- **Problem:** `_xpu_qnorm_rope_kernel` (`vllm/models/deepseek_v4/xpu/xpu_qnorm_rope_kv_fp8_insert.py`) computes `token_idx * num_heads * HEAD_DIM` in int32, so the Q address wraps once a step holds more than 2^31 Q elements (65,536 tokens with 64 local heads); on Intel Arc Pro B60 this ends in `UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST`. The 1M-context DeepSeek-V4 models hit this with a single prompt over 65,536 tokens at TP=1 and `--no-enable-chunked-prefill`. Fixes vllm-project/vllm#52416.\n- **Fix:** promote `token_idx` to int64 (as the sibling DeepSeek-V4 kernels `fused_inv_rope_fp8_quant.py` and `fused_mtp_input_rmsnorm.py` in `vllm/models/deepseek_v4/common/ops/` already do), which also widens the KV offset; `head_idx` stays int32 because `head_idx * HEAD_DIM` is at most 128 × 512. A new regression test calls the public `xpu_qnorm_rope_kv_fp8_insert` op past the boundary, and a new Intel kernels CI step runs it.\n- **Validation:** on Intel Arc Pro B60 with `vllm/vllm-openai-xpu@sha256:14d76dee` (nightly, 2026-10-29) on `main` 5082c45853, `pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v4_xpu_qnorm_rope_large_batch.py -v` gives 1 passed with this PR and 1 failed (`UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST`) without it; below the boundary (4096×64, 8192×8, 8192×64, 32768×16 tokens × heads) Q and the KV cache are bitwise identical to `main` and the op time is within ±0.1%. The new test is short and cheap: a single case on one card, about 15 s for the whole pytest session including the vLLM import (15.5 s with this PR, 16.1 s on `main`), and it needs about 8 GiB of free device memory, skipping otherwise.\n- **Not a duplicate:** this supersedes vllm-project/vllm#52427 (same cast, applied to both program ids, no test; closed by its author on 2026-09-20 without a maintainer review) and adds the regression test and CI step it lacked; no open PR references vllm-project/vllm#52416; vllm-project/vllm#46685 (merged) and vllm-project/vllm#52582 fix the overlapping-store bug in the same kernel and do not touch the index type.\n- **AI assistance:** this PR was written with AI assistance; I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
